# P5.6 wave 3 (w3-slots): the end-of-frame effects drawn by the graph, each a scope of its own: depth of field and the distant
# blur (ISDepthOfField*/ISDistantBlur*, with their compute blurs ISDepthOfFieldBlurH/VCS), refraction, the radial blur, and the
# snow pass's ISCopySubRegionCS. Only these groups are selected, so a difference from imagespace-sao-ssr-org0.env's shots is
# theirs (the distant blur softens the far hills at Whiterun by day). The log should show "[ORG] ImageSpace: on" listing them,
# "registered <n> passes", "the graph holds <n> passes", "the first batch", no "[ORG] ImageSpace:" error and no "is sized for"
# warning. Each refused effect is named once ("<effect> stays on D3D11 (<reason>)"); an effect the tour never reaches (the radial
# blur, refraction) logs nothing. CS_ORG_EPOCH_STATS=1 logs the ImageSpace anchor's peak runs a frame against its 13.
CS_ORG_ENGINE_CONSTANTS=1
CS_ORG_IMAGESPACE=1
CS_ORG_IMAGESPACE_EFFECTS=dof,refraction,radialblur,copy
CS_ORG_IMAGESPACE_LOG=1
CS_ORG_EPOCH_STATS=1
DXVK_DEBUG=hang
VK_LOADER_LAYERS_DISABLE=*nsight*
CS_DCLF_TEST_COMMANDS=600:set timescale to 0;601:set gamehour to 13;602:fw 81a;700:coc Whiterun;2000:fw 81a;2400:dclf:shot=whiterun;2410:set gamehour to 23;2800:dclf:shot=whiterun-night;2810:set gamehour to 13;2900:coc WhiterunDragonsreach;4000:dclf:shot=dragonsreach;4100:coc Riverwood;5200:fw 81a;5500:dclf:shot=riverwood;5510:tfc;5520:dclf:shot=riverwood-tfc
CS_DCLF_TEST_EXIT=5600
